    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Track an object in a local video and generate a complete timestamped mask\r\nsequence without modifying any draft.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input local video file path.\r\n          --seed-time TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Seed frame time in the input video. Bare numbers are seconds;\r\n                              also supports s/ms/us.\r\n          --output-dir TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Existing writable directory for generated rel_json and SAM3\r\n                              Results/RLE JSON files.\r\n          --seed-mask-rle-json, --mask-rle-json TEXT \r\n                              Seed mask RLE JSON object or @path, e.g.\r\n                              {\"counts\":[...],\"size\":[height,width]}.\r\n          --target-object-desc, --sam3-target-object-desc TEXT \r\n                              Target object description for seed mask generation; mutually\r\n                              exclusive with --seed-mask-rle-json.\r\n          --feather TEXT      Feather metadata to return with the seed result, default 0.\r\n          --edge-size, --expansion, --expand TEXT \r\n                              Edge-size metadata to return with the seed result, default 0.\r\n          --reverse           Return reverse=true metadata with the seed result for downstream\r\n                              application.\r\n          --sam3-debug-artifacts \r\n                              Keep extracted seed frame and SAM3 debug JSON files when using\r\n                              --target-object-desc.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Generate rel_json from an externally supplied seed mask RLE\r\n  $ lyra-cli media object-matting-track --input /tmp/clip.mp4 --seed-time 1s \\\r\n      --output-dir /tmp/matting --seed-mask-rle-json '{\"counts\":[2,2],\"size\":[2,2]}' \\\r\n      --feather 0 --edge-size 0\r\n  # Or describe the target object and let lyra-cli generate the seed mask\r\n  $ lyra-cli media object-matting-track --input /tmp/clip.mp4 --seed-time 1s \\\r\n      --output-dir /tmp/matting --target-object-desc \"phone\" --sam3-debug-artifacts\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - This command writes the SAM3 seed artifacts and the propagated VOS mask sequence under --output-dir.\r\n  - It does not accept --ref, --seg-id, or --target and does not modify drafts.\r\n  - --seed-mask-rle-json and --target-object-desc are mutually exclusive.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
